    "https://jobs.uca.edu/postings/19590": {
      "title": "Pre-BSN Student Coordinator",
      "description": "University of Central Arkansas Employment Opportunities | Pre-BSN Student Coordinator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs NEW   Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Pre-BSN Student Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Title Information Full-Time/Part-Time Full Time Salary Range $39,275 Will this position be Onsite, Remote, or Hybrid? Onsite Position Details Position Information Posting Number NC1022026 Working Title Pre-BSN Student Coordinator Department Org 344000 - Nursing Why should you work at UCA? We are excited that you are considering joining the UCA Family—the faculty, staff, students and alumni—who make the University of Central Arkansas a great place to work! At the University of Central Arkansas, we value our employees striving to maintain a work-life balance. We realize that this affects the overall well-being of employees while learning to prioritize challenging work and the ability to make a difference. Participation in university-wide flexible work schedules may be available for certain positions. Training is provided on systems or job-specific software, and tools are available supporting professional and personal development. The benefits package allows you to customize your benefits to meet your current needs, with the ability to adjust them as your priorities change. This includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, 80% tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a retirement program with university contributions of 10% of employee salary. Also available are health and wellness incentives, as well as access to sports and cultural activities on campus for the family, free gym membership and equipment rentals. Position Summary The Pre- BSN Student Coordinator is to assist students in their growth and development by constructing meaningful educational plans which are compatible with their life goals. It is a continuous and consistent process which is built upon the basis of frequent, accumulated personal contacts between advisor and advisee. The Pre- BSN Student Coordinator is responsible for assessing, and counseling individuals and providing individual/group education and vocational guidance services. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy. Job Duties and Responsibilities 1. Pre-Nursing Advising Continuously counsel and advise all UCA undergraduate Pre-Nursing students from the first day of orientation until graduation. Educate Pre-Nursing BSN students, and other potential students, with understanding and scheduling of curriculum, registration, drop/add, university policies, etc. Educate transfer students with understanding and scheduling of curriculum, registration, drop/add, university policies, etc. Educate post-baccalaureate students with understanding and scheduling of curriculum, registration, drop/add, university policies, etc. Develop plans of study for all Pre-Nursing BSN students Guide the Pre- BSN student towards specific goals and objective outcomes. Maintain current knowledge regarding UCA admission, transfer, and degree requirements. Maintain current knowledge regarding Financial Aid requirements to ensure students comply with their scholarship requirements throughout the year. Maintain current knowledge of nursing admissions, information, standards, and other nursing programs in the state of Arkansas. Review test scores/high school GPA and enroll undergraduate Pre- BSN transitional students in courses. Explore options with Pre-Nursing students placed on academic probation, academic alert, and/or academic suspension. Manage the progress of “at-risk” students during the progress report timeline and provide success coaching and additional support to the student. Refer the student to other departments on campus as needed for additional support. Serve as the School of Nursing liaison with fellow academic advisors in support departments regarding prerequisite courses (e.g., Biology, Math, Psychology, etc.). Continuously audit degree progression for potential admission of Pre-Nursing students to ensure all requirements are met ( BSN student audits). Attend Advising Summer Orientation Training Attend UCA Campus Partners monthly meetings. 2. Pre-Nursing Admission Collaborate and review with the School of Nursing Director, Undergraduate Program Coordinator, and Administrative Assistant on the entire admissions process. Assist and review qualifications in the ranking of all qualified and non-qualified Pre-Nursing BSN applicants. Monitor the progression of all Pre-Licensure BSN qualified students to maintain accurate information. Verify data and reports used in the ranking of all Pre-Nursing BSN applicants. Onboard Transfer Students and verify transfer credit and outstanding transcripts in compliance with DegreeWorks. Collaborate with conditionally admitted Pre-Licensure BSN students regarding outstanding prerequisite requirements. Collaborate with the School of Nursing Program Coordinator to aid BSN student progression. Meet with students who are not qualified to attend the Nursing program and discuss alternative options. 3. Sample Degree Plans ( SDP )/Bulletin Updates Contribute to the School of Nursing departmental reports requiring student data and application admission historical data. Coordinate with the School of Nursing Director and Program Coordinator to update Sample Degree Plans ( SDP ) 4. School of Nursing Committees Serve as a member of the SON Faculty Staff Organization – prepare and deliver the Education Counselor Report for the SON faculty and staff. Serve as a member of the Nursing Joint Council – develops, revises, and recommends policies and procedures based on research findings with faculty and staff. Serve as a member of the Nursing Staff Council – serve in an advisor capacity to the Director and SON Staff Serve as permanent members of UGAAA and work on task-force groups as needed. Serve as a member of SON Evaluation and Quality Assurance committee ( EQAC ) and work on task-force groups as needed. Provide weekly updates to the School of Nursing Staff Council 5. Recruitment Create and present at SOAR and Admitted Student Day for the School of Nursing Present at New Student Orientation during Welcome Week for incoming Pre- BSN students Participate in recruitment events such as Bear Facts Day, Bear Fair, and Majors Fair Receive and respond to all pre-licensure inquiries year-round. Ensure all Pre-Nursing advising materials and documents are up to date and complete. Participate in School of Nursing recruitment activities for Pre- BSN students as needed. 6. Collaboration Collaborate with fellow advisors to provide students with information on other programs, interests, and majors at UCA . Develop and foster relationships with College of Health and Behavior Sciences advisors. Network with Nursing Education Counselors from other institutions to assist students with information regarding options for other programs, if needed Network with ROTC to ensure students are fulfilling all requirements. 7. Personal Development Develop and foster relationships both on campus and off campus with other universities, hospitals, and nursing programs. Participate in professional organizations at the state ( ARKAAN ) and national ( NACADA ) level every year for education on current advising practices. Conduct research of interest to the profession & disseminate findings to fellow staff and faculty. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of the organization and administration of higher education. Knowledge of student development theory. Knowledge of policies and procedures relating to admissions and registration. Knowledge of available college and community resources and/or programs. Skill in delivering classroom and public presentations. Skill in prioritizing and managing multiple tasks. Ability to work collaboratively and independently with common goals as a part of a team. Ability to make sound judgments and assist in resolving student concerns. Ability to defuse an emotional or tense situation and offer viable solutions. Ability to work with diverse students. Ability to effectively communicate in oral and written form. Civility in all interactions of a public or confidential nature. Positive attitude and willingness to help students be successful. Skills Considered Essential for Success -Knowledge of the organization and administration of higher education. -Knowledge of state, federal, and university rules, regulations and procedures. -Ability to work in a diverse and dynamic environment. -Ability to work collaboratively and independently with common goals as a part of a team. -Ability to make sound judgments. -Effective interpersonal communication, writing, and organizational abilities. -Civility in all interactions. -Demonstrate effective follow-up. Required Education and/or Experience The formal education equivalent of a master’s degree in student affairs, education, counseling, communication, psychology, or related field. Additional requirements determined by the agency for recruiting purposes require review and approval by the Office of Personnel Management. OTHER JOB - RELATED EDUCATION AND /OR EXPERIENCE MAY BE SUBSTITUTED FOR ALL OR PART OF THESE BASIC REQUIREMENTS , EXCEPT FOR CERTIFICATION OR LICENSURE REQUIREMENTS , UPON APPROVAL OF THE QUALIFICATIONS REVIEW COMMITTEE . Preferred Education and/or Experience These qualification and characteristics are critical to success in this important role in the UCA School of Nursing. Please clarify in your application materials the experiences, successes, and techniques evidencing how you bring these strengths: Master’s Degree in student affairs, education, counseling, communication, psychology, or related field and one year of experience in counseling or a related field OR demonstration of knowledge of student development/student retention theory and best practices. Demonstrated experience working with diverse populations, including but not limited to students of color, individuals who are non-native English speakers, individuals with pre-college academic skills, first generation college students, and individuals experiencing disability. Demonstrated commitment to student success through application of holistic, developmental, and personalized advising strategies. Considerable knowledge of and experience practicing inclusive, culturally responsive, and unbiased service delivery. Demonstrated understanding of advising philosophies, and theoretical frameworks, such as NACADA Core Values, and CAS Standards of Advising. Strong public speaking, presentation, and interpersonal communication skills. Strong organizational, time management, and task management skills. Ability to use current and new technology effectively to support advising related activities including accessing data, connecting with students, and managing records. University, Campus, and Community Description Thank you for your interest in employment at the University of Central Arkansas. Founded in 1907, UCA has an enrollment of more than 10,000 students and employs over 1,300 full-time employees. The university offers more than 85 undergraduate and 59 graduate certificate and degree programs, including doctoral programs in five disciplines. UCA is proud of its tradition of teaching excellence and its contributions in research, scholarship, and creative activities. Desired start date 08/16/2026 Position Summary and Qualifications License(s)/Certifications Not required Physical Demands Checklist Sitting, Standing, Lifting/Carrying, Walking Physical Exertion Administrative Work - Exerting up to 10 pounds, Light Work - Exerting up to 20 pounds Posting Detail Information Background Check Statement This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal, sex-offender registry, financial history background check and drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. UCA EEO Statement The University of Central Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. In keeping with its nondiscrimination policy in employment, admissions and other functions and programs, the university considers employees and students on the basis of individual merit and will not discriminate against a person on the basis of gender, race or color, ethnicity, religion, spiritual beliefs, national origin, age, familial status, socioeconomic background, sexual orientation, disability, political beliefs, intellectual perspective, genetic information, military status, or other factors irrelevant to participation in its programs. Open Date 08/18/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Veteran's Documents Other Document Additional Documents University of Central Arkansas Human Resources 201 Donaghey Ave. Wingo Hall Conway, AR 72035 1.501.450.3181 1.501.450.5088 (fax) humanresources@uca.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uca.edu/postings/18783": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "University of Central Arkansas Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor - School of Nursing Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs NEW   Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor - School of Nursing Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Submit a cover letter outlining how you meet the requirements and preferences for the position, curriculum vitae, and names of three references with contact information (loaded under “other documents”) via the university online employment at https://jobs.uca.edu . Position Details Position Information Posting Number F0112026 Working Title Assistant Professor - School of Nursing Department Org 344000 - Nursing Why should you work at UCA? We are excited that you are considering joining the UCA Family—the faculty, staff, students and alumni—who make the University of Central Arkansas a great place to work! At the University of Central Arkansas, we value our employees striving to maintain a work-life balance. We realize that this affects the overall well-being of employees while learning to prioritize challenging work and the ability to make a difference. Participation in university-wide flexible work schedules may be available for certain positions. Training is provided on systems or job-specific software, and tools are available supporting professional and personal development. The benefits package allows you to customize your benefits to meet your current needs, with the ability to adjust them as your priorities change. This includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, 80% tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a retirement program with university contributions of 10% of employee salary. Also available are health and wellness incentives, as well as access to sports and cultural activities on campus for the family, free gym membership and equipment rentals. Position Summary The University of Central Arkansas ( UCA ) is seeking a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor (9-month appointment) to join the School of Nursing. This on-campus role is designed for a doctorally prepared ( DNP or PhD) Family Nurse Practitioner who will shape the next generation of nursing professionals. The successful candidate will lead innovative educational programs, conduct scholarly research, and contribute to a supportive, inclusive academic environment. Learn more at: www.uca.edu/nursing Job Duties and Responsibilities This tenure track position focuses on teaching, curriculum development, assessment and evaluation, collaboration and mentorship. The faculty member will facilitate student learning, engage in research and scholarship, focus on continuous professional development and provide institutional, professional and community service. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities As a tenure-track faculty, you will translate intricate clinical data into digestible, evidence-based instruction. You will ground your teaching in the current realities of healthcare policy and ethics, ensuring students are equipped to navigate the systemic challenges of modern healthcare. Key Responsibilities: Curriculum Innovation: Design and deliver high-impact programs utilizing active learning and high-fidelity simulations. Mentorship & Leadership: Guide novice nurses and colleagues through the nuances of clinical judgment and professional identity. Interdisciplinary Collaboration: Thrive within academic teams to drive institutional excellence and adapt to evolving accreditation standards. Scholarly Contribution: Advance the profession through reflective practice, original research, and advocacy for healthcare equity. Qualifications & Skills: Clinical Mastery: Advanced knowledge of nursing science and delivery systems. Instructional Excellence: Proven ability to apply educational theory to clinical complexity. Dynamic Communication: Exceptional interpersonal skills with the ability to lead and inspire. Adaptability: A commitment to lifelong learning and the integration of emerging healthcare technologies. Skills Considered Essential for Success -Knowledge of the organization and administration of higher education. -Knowledge of state, federal, and university rules, regulations and procedures. -Ability to work in a diverse and dynamic environment. -Ability to work collaboratively and independently with common goals as a part of a team. -Ability to make sound judgments. -Effective interpersonal communication, writing, and organizational abilities. -Civility in all interactions. -Demonstrate effective follow-up. Required Education and/or Experience The candidate MUST have: 1) Doctoral degree (PhD in Nursing or DNP from a nationally accredited institution. 2) APRN certification and licensure as a Family Nurse Practitioner and current unencumbered RN license. 3) Significant clinical experience in nursing practice. 4) Prior experience teaching nursing students at the undergraduate and/or graduate level, with a strong understanding of pedagogical principles and instructional methodologies. Candidates who are ABD or who have 3 or less semesters left to complete the doctoral degree will be considered. Must have all clinical requirements mandated by the clinical agencies used for student clinical experiences. These requirements include: 1) MMR (2 vaccines or a positive titer), 2) Varicella (2 vaccines at least 28 days apart or positive titer), 3) Hepatitis B (2 part series or positive surface antibodies above 10), 4) Tdap (must be received within the last 10 years), 5) Tb (Initial testing: Interferon-gamma release assay ( IGRA ) or a tuberculin skin test ( TST ) for persons without documented prior testing, TB disease or latent TB infection ( LTBI ). Retesting: No annual retest or routine serial testing at any interval after baseline in the absence of a known exposure or ongoing transmission is required), 6) Infuenza vaccine (annually); and 7) current CPR certification BLS from American Health Association. Preferred Education and/or Experience It is PREFERRED that the candidate has: 1) Educational preparation as a nurse educator or experience teaching at the undergraduate or graduate level. 2) Experience with learning management systems and/or online teaching at the baccalaureate or higher degree. 3) Experience with simulation teaching at the baccalaureate level or higher. 4) Candidates with current practice experience. License(s)/Certifications (Required or Preferred) Compact RN license in Arkansas. APRN certification and licensure as a Family Nurse Practitioner. University, Campus, and Community Description Thank you for your interest in employment at the University of Central Arkansas. Founded in 1907, UCA has an enrollment of more than 10,000 students and employs over 1,300 full-time employees. The university offers more than 85 undergraduate and 59 graduate certificate and degree programs, including doctoral programs in five disciplines. UCA is proud of its tradition of teaching excellence and its contributions in research, scholarship, and creative activities. Desired start date 08/16/2026 Will this position be Onsite, Remote, or Hybrid? Onsite Posting Detail Information Background Check Statement This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal, sex-offender registry, financial history background check and drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. UCA EEO Statement The University of Central Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. In keeping with its nondiscrimination policy in employment, admissions and other functions and programs, the university considers employees and students on the basis of individual merit and will not discriminate against a person on the basis of gender, race or color, ethnicity, religion, spiritual beliefs, national origin, age, familial status, socioeconomic background, sexual orientation, disability, political beliefs, intellectual perspective, genetic information, military status, or other factors irrelevant to participation in its programs. Open Date 03/24/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Submit a cover letter outlining how you meet the requirements and preferences for the position, curriculum vitae, and names of three references with contact information (loaded under “other documents”) via the university online employment at https://jobs.uca.edu . Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Unofficial Transcripts Other Document License or Certification Other Transcripts Veteran's Documents Additional Documents University of Central Arkansas Human Resources 201 Donaghey Ave. Wingo Hall Conway, AR 72035 1.501.450.3181 1.501.450.5088 (fax) humanresources@uca.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uca.edu/postings/19710": {
      "title": "Position Details",
      "description": "University of Central Arkansas Employment Opportunities | Fiscal Support Analyst Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs NEW   Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Fiscal Support Analyst Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Title Information Full-Time/Part-Time Full Time Salary Range $31,200 Will this position be Onsite, Remote, or Hybrid? Onsite Position Details Position Information Posting Number NC1112026 Working Title Fiscal Support Analyst Department Org 335000 - Music Why should you work at UCA? We are excited that you are considering joining the UCA Family—the faculty, staff, students and alumni—who make the University of Central Arkansas a great place to work! At the University of Central Arkansas, we value our employees striving to maintain a work-life balance. We realize that this affects the overall well-being of employees while learning to prioritize challenging work and the ability to make a difference. Participation in university-wide flexible work schedules may be available for certain positions. Training is provided on systems or job-specific software, and tools are available supporting professional and personal development. The benefits package allows you to customize your benefits to meet your current needs, with the ability to adjust them as your priorities change. This includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, 80% tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a retirement program with university contributions of 10% of employee salary. Also available are health and wellness incentives, as well as access to sports and cultural activities on campus for the family, free gym membership and equipment rentals. Position Summary The Fiscal Support Analyst is responsible for performing a wide variety of fiscal related tasks that are standard or regular support duties within an assigned department or program and for researching financial data and preparing reports. This position is governed by Generally Accepted Accounting Principles, state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy. Apply at jobs.uca.edu. Job Duties and Responsibilities Researches and analyzes data, develops or revise processes or policies based on research, and submits prepared report findings to supervisor. Develops and maintains databases, spreadsheets and other fiscal reporting mechanisms, reviews and audits fiscal information for accuracy and quality assurance. Provides technical assistance to others working within various databases and systems, including the state accounting system and general ledger, and assists in reconciling problems. Posts transactions to journals and/or ledgers, balances entries, and reconciles errors manually or electronically. Performs various accounting duties and assists with budgets and fiscal monthly and year end closing. Produces monthly production reports, statistical reports, or other regularly scheduled reports. May be responsible for proper and timely entry of time records, payroll related documents, purchase orders, personnel action forms, budget documents, labor distribution reports, or any other procedural forms required by other departments or divisions. May serve as a lead worker, providing training and guidance to fellow employees and establishing work plans, timeframes and/or deadlines or may supervise a small support staff by interviewing, training, assigning and reviewing work, and evaluating performance. Performs other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of accounting principals and database management. Knowledge of software applications. Knowledge of applicable laws, regulations, and policies of assigned section. Knowledge of customer service techniques. Ability to comprehend and assimilate technical and business related documents. Ability to apply policies and procedures and other applicable regulations associated with assigned department or program. Ability to conduct research, perform quantitative quality assurance reviews, and prepare reports. Skills Considered Essential for Success -Knowledge of the organization and administration of higher education. -Knowledge of state, federal, and university rules, regulations and procedures. -Ability to work in a diverse and dynamic environment. -Ability to work collaboratively and independently with common goals as a part of a team. -Ability to make sound judgments. -Effective interpersonal communication, writing, and organizational abilities. -Civility in all interactions. -Demonstrate effective follow-up. Required Education and/or Experience The formal education equivalent of a bachelor’s degree in general business, finance, or a related field. Preferred Education and/or Experience University, Campus, and Community Description Thank you for your interest in employment at the University of Central Arkansas. Founded in 1907, UCA has an enrollment of more than 10,000 students and employs over 1,300 full-time employees. The university offers more than 85 undergraduate and 59 graduate certificate and degree programs, including doctoral programs in five disciplines. UCA is proud of its tradition of teaching excellence and its contributions in research, scholarship, and creative activities. Desired start date 09/16/2026 Position Summary and Qualifications License(s)/Certifications Physical Demands Checklist Sitting, Standing, Lifting/Carrying, Walking Physical Exertion Light Work - Exerting up to 20 pounds Posting Detail Information Background Check Statement This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal, sex-offender registry, financial history background check and drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. UCA EEO Statement The University of Central Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. In keeping with its nondiscrimination policy in employment, admissions and other functions and programs, the university considers employees and students on the basis of individual merit and will not discriminate against a person on the basis of gender, race or color, ethnicity, religion, spiritual beliefs, national origin, age, familial status, socioeconomic background, sexual orientation, disability, political beliefs, intellectual perspective, genetic information, military status, or other factors irrelevant to participation in its programs. Open Date 09/04/2026 Close Date 09/11/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Veteran's Documents Other Document University of Central Arkansas Human Resources 201 Donaghey Ave. Wingo Hall Conway, AR 72035 1.501.450.3181 1.501.450.5088 (fax) humanresources@uca.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
